  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1228 AM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nFriday a weak upper ridge will build over the region and dry weather \nwill continue. Friday morning will be much cooler with the dry \nairmass in place. Highs Friday will be about the same as Thursday. \nFriday night the upper ridge will get pushed to the east as another \ntrough digs into the southwest. The old frontal boundary will still \nbe in the vicinity. The combination of the upper trough and surface \nboundary will bring chances for rain for the weekend. Rain chances \nwill spread across from west to east beginning Friday night out \nwest. They will cover the area Saturday and move off to the east \nSunday. An upper level ridge will move in starting Monday bringing \ndry weather back for the first couple of days of next week. At this \ntime, rainfall totals over the weekend look moderate with no \nsignificant impacts.\n\nWith cloudy skies and showers, temperatures will be cooler over the \nweekend. After the rain moves away Monday winds will become \nnortheasterly bringing in cooler, drier air. Temperatures Monday and \nTuesday will be a few degrees cooler than the weekend.",
